{
  "_comment": [
    "What the stub model answers, one rule per document. First match wins.",
    "",
    "Five documents, because a Jira source produces two kinds: four issues, and",
    "the one file PLAY-1 carries. `document` is the ledger key, and the key of a",
    "file is `<issue>/<filename>` (R1.6) -- a stage is shown the key it must",
    "carry back (R3.13), so these strings are not decoration.",
    "",
    "`match` is a list of substrings that must all appear in the rendered prompt.",
    "`# PLAY-1 ` with the trailing space is what tells PLAY-1 from PLAY-1001: the",
    "issue's heading is written by the playground converter from `key` and",
    "`summary`, and the attachment's is the corpus note's own first line.",
    "",
    "Every `span` appears verbatim in the document it names -- that is what makes",
    "the field grounded (R6.4). The issue and its attachment repeat some spans",
    "because Jira holds the same sentence twice, and each is grounded in its own",
    "document.",
    "",
    "The keys assume a project seeded into an empty Jira, where PLAY numbers from",
    "1. If your instance had already issued PLAY keys, renumber the `match` and",
    "`document` values to what `dossier sync` actually reported."
  ],
  "rules": [
    {
      "match": ["# PLAY-1001"],
      "reply": {
        "document": "PLAY-1/postmortem.md",
        "fields": [
          {
            "field": "loss_amount",
            "value": 18400.0,
            "currency": "CHF",
            "confidence": "high",
            "source": {
              "document": "PLAY-1/postmortem.md",
              "span": "a recorded loss of CHF 18'400"
            }
          },
          {
            "field": "resolution_date",
            "value": "2026-03-04",
            "confidence": "high",
            "source": {"document": "PLAY-1/postmortem.md", "span": "**Resolved:** 2026-03-04"}
          },
          {
            "field": "severity",
            "value": "major",
            "confidence": "high",
            "source": {"document": "PLAY-1/postmortem.md", "span": "**Severity:** major"}
          },
          {
            "field": "affected_systems",
